Constant agent-agnostic PR monitor, built on the #366 verdict core. PR-A of the
split (PR-B adds the watch streaming loop + ship lifecycle hook).

Gather completeness (audit A5/A6) — fills the gaps left after #366:
- adapter.fetchBase({baseRef,cwd}): git-fetch the base ref, wired into
  gatherPrSnapshot BEFORE readDivergence/detectConflicts so they compare against
  the CURRENT origin/<base>, not a stale local ref (false behind=0 / no-conflict).
- isFailed now covers STALE (a stale required CheckRun no longer pends forever).
- readIssueComments surfaces a stable comment id (fullDatabaseId) for event dedup.
(readReviews, reviewDecision, isDraft, author-agnostic paginated issue comments,
isOutdated threads, ERROR/STARTUP_FAILURE were already added by #366.)

One gather + one verdict core:
- Extract gatherPrSnapshot(ctx) from gatherPullSignal — the shared read+verdict
  the monitor diffs, so verdict and events can never disagree. gatherPullSignal
  keeps only its bounded --pull projection (behaviour unchanged).

Monitor (lib/pr-monitor/):
- events.js: schema {v,seq,ts,repo,pr,headSha,type,key,data,verdict}, content-keyed
  identity, deterministic fingerprint.
- differ.js: pure diffSnapshots(prev,next) — every event type on its transition.
- journal.js: per-PR append-only NDJSON + atomic snapshot fingerprint under
  .forge/pr-monitor/<repo>-<pr>/; seq/seen-identity dedup; pid helpers.
- gather.js: normalize gatherPrSnapshot into the diff subject.
- monitor.js: runMonitorPass (gather->diff->dedup->append->persist; crash-safe,
  no dupes across restarts) + pollEvents (inline pass when no watcher).
- forge shepherd events <pr> --since <seq> [--json]: agent-agnostic pull surface,
  stdout NDJSON, nothing under .claude/*.

Kernel: c2d398e5 (epic), 9af1ee0a (audit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
